+Reconciled against README.md (the current public API contract) — this note supersedes the earlier one, which was stale.
+
+Contract: `total(prices, discount_percent=0)` where `discount_percent` is a
+PERCENTAGE from 0 through 100 inclusive. Values outside that range raise ValueError.
+
+Earlier note (now WRONG) claimed it was a fraction 0–1 and that the code was
+correct / only the README needed updating. That was backwards: the README already
+documents the percentage contract, so the implementation was the bug.
+
+Fixed in billing.py:
+  - treats `discount_percent` as a percentage (divides by 100), not a fraction
+  - validates `0 <= discount_percent <= 100`, else ValueError
+
+Tests in tests/test_billing.py cover: no discount, partial discount, full
+discount (100), and ValueError for >100 and <0. Run: `python -m pytest -q tests`
+(see README_TESTS.md). All 5 pass.
